1
00:00:17,145 --> 00:00:19,570
[SPEAKER_02]: So, this is the Sabha Sutta.

2
00:00:21,695 --> 00:00:24,241
[SPEAKER_02]: The Blessed One said, what is the All?

3
00:00:25,523 --> 00:00:27,227
[SPEAKER_02]: Simply the I and forms.

4
00:00:28,443 --> 00:00:29,824
[SPEAKER_02]: Ear and sounds.

5
00:00:30,904 --> 00:00:33,185
[SPEAKER_02]: Nose and smells.

6
00:00:33,245 --> 00:00:34,806
[SPEAKER_02]: Tongue, flavor.

7
00:00:36,046 --> 00:00:37,747
[SPEAKER_02]: Body and touches.

8
00:00:38,807 --> 00:00:40,988
[SPEAKER_02]: And mano and dhammas.

9
00:00:42,289 --> 00:00:44,289
[SPEAKER_02]: So, mano... Intellect.

10
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:45,390
[SPEAKER_02]: Intellect, yeah.

11
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,571
[SPEAKER_02]: And dhammas, images...

12
00:00:47,591 --> 00:00:48,251
[SPEAKER_02]: Images, phenomena.

13
00:00:48,331 --> 00:00:48,651
[SPEAKER_02]: Thoughts.

14
00:00:49,011 --> 00:00:51,152
[SPEAKER_02]: Thoughts, sure.

15
00:00:51,172 --> 00:00:53,393
[SPEAKER_02]: So, intellect and thoughts.

16
00:00:55,754 --> 00:00:57,915
[SPEAKER_02]: This, monks, is called the all.

17
00:00:59,494 --> 00:01:05,497
[SPEAKER_02]: Anyone who would say, rejecting this all, I will make known another.

18
00:01:05,997 --> 00:01:06,658
[SPEAKER_02]: All.

19
00:01:06,738 --> 00:01:06,898
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

20
00:01:07,098 --> 00:01:07,638
[SPEAKER_02]: A new all.

21
00:01:07,678 --> 00:01:08,839
[SPEAKER_02]: I will describe another one.

22
00:01:09,019 --> 00:01:11,440
[SPEAKER_04]: Something... A higher reality than this.

23
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,120
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

24
00:01:13,601 --> 00:01:21,825
[SPEAKER_02]: If questioned on what exactly might be the grounds for your statement, he would be unable to explain and furthermore get frustrated.

25
00:01:23,915 --> 00:01:24,155
[SPEAKER_02]: Why?

26
00:01:24,255 --> 00:01:27,157
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that is not his domain.

27
00:01:27,918 --> 00:01:29,619
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not his personal scope.

28
00:01:29,899 --> 00:01:31,360
[SPEAKER_02]: He cannot know that.

29
00:01:33,682 --> 00:01:38,566
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, whatever that new or old he might be describing, it will be within any one of those.

30
00:01:39,486 --> 00:01:43,089
[SPEAKER_04]: Cannot be anything apart from the sixth sense base.

31
00:01:43,929 --> 00:01:44,590
[SPEAKER_04]: Inconceivable.

32
00:01:45,247 --> 00:01:46,648
[SPEAKER_04]: I mean, you say, no, no, this is apart from it.

33
00:01:46,668 --> 00:01:48,829
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, you're just describing another image to me.

34
00:01:48,849 --> 00:01:49,589
[SPEAKER_02]: That is part of it.

35
00:01:49,709 --> 00:01:53,571
[SPEAKER_02]: I can describe another, or all that I... that you believe.

36
00:01:53,891 --> 00:01:54,952
[SPEAKER_04]: You believe in, imagine.

37
00:01:55,032 --> 00:01:57,353
[SPEAKER_04]: Ignoring the fact that, exactly, you imagine it.

38
00:01:57,733 --> 00:01:59,474
[SPEAKER_04]: It's real as imagination, sure.

39
00:01:59,594 --> 00:02:01,455
[SPEAKER_04]: As images, as phenomena, it is real.

40
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:03,616
[SPEAKER_04]: And thus, it's very much within this all.

41
00:02:05,256 --> 00:02:12,920
[SPEAKER_04]: But you claiming that it's beyond the six senses, while using the six senses to describe it and refer to it, or even just think of it,

42
00:02:13,971 --> 00:02:16,112
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, that's a contradiction in terms for that very reason.

43
00:02:16,993 --> 00:02:20,215
[SPEAKER_04]: How can you then designate the all, if you can't even think it?

44
00:02:21,676 --> 00:02:22,597
[SPEAKER_03]: What are you designating?

45
00:02:22,817 --> 00:02:23,577
[SPEAKER_03]: What are you talking about?

46
00:02:26,719 --> 00:02:31,202
[SPEAKER_04]: That's what people say, like, well, you know, you can't... you can't really describe God.

47
00:02:32,303 --> 00:02:33,804
[SPEAKER_04]: It's like, well, you just described it.

48
00:02:35,004 --> 00:02:36,205
[SPEAKER_04]: That's exactly a description.

49
00:02:37,246 --> 00:02:38,307
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, it's indescribable.

50
00:02:39,427 --> 00:02:42,109
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, that's a property of God, which is then describable.

51
00:02:44,953 --> 00:02:46,994
[SPEAKER_04]: So, then it's a contradiction in terms, such a statement.

52
00:02:49,175 --> 00:02:56,117
[SPEAKER_02]: So, here we got that, that common view, which is, there is something beyond all the aggregates.

53
00:02:56,557 --> 00:02:56,817
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

54
00:02:57,157 --> 00:03:02,399
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, that ground of being, that unity of... Self.

55
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:04,120
[SPEAKER_02]: Unity of self.

56
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,060
[SPEAKER_02]: With a higher self.

57
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:05,401
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

58
00:03:05,501 --> 00:03:09,542
[SPEAKER_02]: That, yeah, one, non, non-dual, I suppose.

59
00:03:11,563 --> 00:03:12,063
[SPEAKER_02]: Consciousness.

60
00:03:13,988 --> 00:03:16,209
[SPEAKER_02]: It never changes.

61
00:03:16,249 --> 00:03:16,389
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

62
00:03:16,609 --> 00:03:17,489
[SPEAKER_02]: All the names you can...

63
00:03:18,229 --> 00:03:19,609
[SPEAKER_02]: But how do you know that?

64
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:21,290
[SPEAKER_04]: Because you have images of it.

65
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:21,590
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

66
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:22,530
[SPEAKER_02]: Because I have a thought about it.

67
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:23,050
[SPEAKER_04]: Which are changing.

68
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:24,070
[SPEAKER_02]: Which is... Yeah.

69
00:03:24,931 --> 00:03:25,791
[SPEAKER_03]: So, I'm still stuck.

70
00:03:25,811 --> 00:03:38,634
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you're ignoring what's right in front of you and reinterpreting everything from this internal, obviously, you cannot be outside of your aggregates, but externally assumed universe and world and point of view.

71
00:03:40,032 --> 00:03:42,274
[SPEAKER_04]: And in a nutshell, that's the definition of attavāda.

72
00:03:42,774 --> 00:03:53,241
[SPEAKER_04]: Assuming that you can be out, don't matter what view you have, what interpretation, what description, whether you're talking about anicca or the universal ātman, it doesn't matter.

73
00:03:54,081 --> 00:03:57,684
[SPEAKER_04]: If there is an attitude of... from the outside, that's attavāda.

74
00:03:58,604 --> 00:04:00,706
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if you don't think necessarily in terms of self.

75
00:04:01,066 --> 00:04:05,229
[SPEAKER_02]: Unique, independent... Means, basically, outside point of view.

76
00:04:05,529 --> 00:04:07,110
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's an internal image.

77
00:04:08,302 --> 00:04:10,664
[SPEAKER_04]: Which you realize, oh, that's why it's a contradiction in terms.

78
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:18,629
[SPEAKER_04]: So, whenever you think outside, it's done with mano and intellect, which is six sense bases, which means it's inside of this all.

79
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:24,143
[SPEAKER_02]: So, is there a thing beyond the aggregates or beyond experience?

80
00:04:25,143 --> 00:04:28,105
[SPEAKER_02]: And you just answer, no, there's nothing like that.

81
00:04:28,745 --> 00:04:31,927
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, no, see, that's already... there's nothing.

82
00:04:32,308 --> 00:04:35,790
[SPEAKER_04]: You just made it into something.

83
00:04:35,810 --> 00:04:43,775
[SPEAKER_04]: Theoretically, there is nothing, but you have to realize that, like, theory, it's always going to be on a level of review.

84
00:04:44,135 --> 00:04:48,338
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you can have the right theory, but even then, it will remain on the level of review, which means

85
00:04:49,158 --> 00:04:50,019
[SPEAKER_04]: It's not true for you.

86
00:04:50,199 --> 00:04:51,240
[SPEAKER_04]: You need to start doing it.

87
00:04:52,181 --> 00:04:52,901
[SPEAKER_04]: So, when you make a...

88
00:04:53,062 --> 00:04:54,703
[SPEAKER_04]: So, I must never make a statement there is nothing.

89
00:04:54,723 --> 00:04:54,843
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

90
00:04:54,883 --> 00:04:59,787
[SPEAKER_04]: Make a statement there is nothing, but then include it rightly in the all that is here and now.

91
00:04:59,968 --> 00:05:00,888
[SPEAKER_04]: And that is your practice.

92
00:05:00,908 --> 00:05:01,669
[SPEAKER_04]: That is your bhāvana.

93
00:05:01,689 --> 00:05:02,950
[SPEAKER_04]: That is your right all that... That is your doing.

94
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:08,355
[SPEAKER_04]: ...right contradiction... your right... rightly arranged things that will be then freeing you from these contradictions.

95
00:05:09,756 --> 00:05:10,277
[SPEAKER_04]: Assumptions.

96
00:05:10,737 --> 00:05:11,578
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

97
00:05:11,658 --> 00:05:13,880
[SPEAKER_04]: Every assumption is... has to be a contradiction in itself.

98
00:05:14,942 --> 00:05:19,144
[SPEAKER_04]: Not that you necessarily see it that way initially, but that's the whole point.

99
00:05:19,244 --> 00:05:27,907
[SPEAKER_04]: Assumption of external self, assumption of the views coming, like, as the determining factor for everything else, ignoring the reality upon which they exist.

100
00:05:31,828 --> 00:05:43,333
[SPEAKER_02]: So, I can have an imagination, a fantastic imagination of consciousness, some light or whatever, some image of the ground of being or whatever.

101
00:05:46,619 --> 00:05:53,748
[SPEAKER_02]: And then I can just devote myself to that and abandon all of this lesser stuff.

102
00:05:54,048 --> 00:05:54,348
[SPEAKER_04]: Sure.

103
00:05:54,909 --> 00:05:56,070
[SPEAKER_02]: Lesser consciousnesses.

104
00:05:56,431 --> 00:05:56,751
[SPEAKER_02]: Sure.

105
00:05:57,072 --> 00:05:57,432
[SPEAKER_02]: Whatever.

106
00:05:58,293 --> 00:06:01,377
[SPEAKER_02]: And, you know, get quite far and

107
00:06:02,593 --> 00:06:04,534
