371
00:24:53,510 --> 00:24:55,192
[SPEAKER_04]: You need khanti to bear elements.

372
00:24:55,392 --> 00:24:56,913
[SPEAKER_04]: You need to be patient.

373
00:24:56,933 --> 00:25:00,856
[SPEAKER_04]: So, basically, any of these sabhās, savasūtā, you need khanti for.

374
00:25:01,156 --> 00:25:03,458
[SPEAKER_04]: For development, for abandoning, for avoiding.

375
00:25:03,778 --> 00:25:05,400
[SPEAKER_04]: You need to be patient first.

376
00:25:06,212 --> 00:25:20,342
[SPEAKER_04]: To discern, like for hindrances, as we spoke before, when hindrances arise, sensuality or real will, if you're habitual, I get rid of this, I think the opposite, I do this, I do that, you're not very patient, aren't you?

377
00:25:20,382 --> 00:25:21,403
[SPEAKER_04]: What's the problem of...

378
00:25:21,743 --> 00:25:22,724
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm not welcoming this.

379
00:25:23,684 --> 00:25:24,705
[SPEAKER_04]: I didn't make it arise.

380
00:25:26,286 --> 00:25:30,029
[SPEAKER_04]: Why do I need to do the work of removing it, making it go away?

381
00:25:30,907 --> 00:25:33,107
[SPEAKER_04]: No, I'll just be patient and let it go away.

382
00:25:33,567 --> 00:25:38,048
[SPEAKER_03]: And when it sees that I'm not reaching out and interfering, means it's going to lose interest in me.

383
00:25:39,649 --> 00:25:46,710
[SPEAKER_04]: See, if I come to provoke you, you could be... or get a reaction, I don't care what type of reaction it's going to be.

384
00:25:46,890 --> 00:25:50,711
[SPEAKER_04]: Mahārāja doesn't care whether you're going to like him or hate him, as long as you give him a reaction.

385
00:25:51,931 --> 00:25:57,972
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's exactly every time... there was exactly the description for every time in the suttas when Mahārāja was there tempting.

386
00:25:59,952 --> 00:26:06,725
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm trying, I've been trying for six, seven years following him like like a crow just to pick on a piece of fat that dropped out or something.

387
00:26:06,825 --> 00:26:09,230
[SPEAKER_04]: There's nothing, nothing left for me to grab on.

388
00:26:09,290 --> 00:26:10,613
[SPEAKER_04]: So, so he left him alone.

389
00:26:12,582 --> 00:26:16,644
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's the only way Mara has of remaining unseen.

390
00:26:16,864 --> 00:26:17,004
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

391
00:26:17,024 --> 00:26:19,405
[SPEAKER_04]: Because... Well, that's the only way Mara has power over you.

392
00:26:20,205 --> 00:26:20,745
[SPEAKER_04]: If you react.

393
00:26:21,086 --> 00:26:22,406
[SPEAKER_04]: If you go out in his domain.

394
00:26:22,506 --> 00:26:23,347
[SPEAKER_04]: He said that.

395
00:26:23,387 --> 00:26:24,027
[SPEAKER_04]: The Buddha said that.

396
00:26:24,047 --> 00:26:29,069
[SPEAKER_04]: He says Mara does with people what he wants because people take what belongs to Mara.

397
00:26:29,209 --> 00:26:31,290
[SPEAKER_04]: They go there in Mara's domain.

398
00:26:31,410 --> 00:26:33,611
[SPEAKER_04]: What are the things that belong to Mara?

399
00:26:34,711 --> 00:26:34,971
[SPEAKER_04]: The all.

400
00:26:34,991 --> 00:26:36,912
[SPEAKER_04]: The all belongs to Māra.

401
00:26:37,793 --> 00:26:46,977
[SPEAKER_04]: So, if you react, act, interfere, engage with the all, Māra controls you to that extent, because you are the one who took what doesn't belong to you.

402
00:26:47,697 --> 00:26:55,461
[SPEAKER_01]: Whereas, if you're patient, or you practice this endurance, then it's possible to then discern the nature of

403
00:26:56,624 --> 00:26:57,985
[SPEAKER_01]: That image or that phenomena.

404
00:26:58,225 --> 00:26:58,465
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

405
00:26:58,505 --> 00:26:59,405
[SPEAKER_04]: Because it's enduring.

406
00:26:59,646 --> 00:26:59,946
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

407
00:26:59,986 --> 00:27:10,371
[SPEAKER_04]: Having said that, I think, since we qualified that when we say endurance, we mean khanti, and people tend to confuse that for bearing of pahātava, it can be other way around as well.

408
00:27:11,191 --> 00:27:18,215
[SPEAKER_04]: Sometimes people say, oh, this is the khanti of endurance by simply bearing random things and expecting them to go away.

409
00:27:18,675 --> 00:27:21,937
[SPEAKER_04]: See, expecting things to go away means you're still impatient.

410
00:27:22,886 --> 00:27:30,496
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you're enduring things on physical level, you're bearing things on physical level, you might not be acting out, but mentally, you're not patient.

411
00:27:30,776 --> 00:27:33,840
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not accepting the fact that there ever is an enduring.

412
00:27:34,001 --> 00:27:35,643
[SPEAKER_04]: You're still trying to get rid of them.

413
00:27:36,673 --> 00:27:41,754
[SPEAKER_04]: And now you're using patience as a wishful thinking that it will go away on its own.

414
00:27:41,834 --> 00:27:43,095
[SPEAKER_04]: It will go away on its own.

415
00:27:43,735 --> 00:27:47,556
[SPEAKER_04]: But see, you leaning towards it going away means you're not truly patient.

416
00:27:48,076 --> 00:27:53,818
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not truly equanimous towards this thing, whether it's here or not.

417
00:27:54,198 --> 00:27:54,718
[SPEAKER_04]: I don't mind.

418
00:27:54,998 --> 00:27:56,698
[SPEAKER_04]: I am safe with my limbs retract.

419
00:27:57,038 --> 00:28:02,520
[SPEAKER_04]: I am not bothered with the fact that there is an angry person threatening and shouting at me through this door.

420
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:06,246
[SPEAKER_04]: Because I have understood now that he cannot cross this line.

421
00:28:06,727 --> 00:28:09,713
[SPEAKER_04]: And I understood that because I've been patient sufficiently enough.

422
00:28:09,953 --> 00:28:13,160
[SPEAKER_04]: I endured things on the right level sufficiently enough.

423
00:28:15,631 --> 00:28:24,637
[SPEAKER_02]: The sign of you, that you're doing it right, it's always in the suttas that it says, his mind is elevated, and he's internally calm.

424
00:28:24,998 --> 00:28:25,918
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's another thing.

425
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:32,483
[SPEAKER_02]: With that thing in front of him there, with that monster there, his mind is elevated and internally calm.

426
00:28:32,503 --> 00:28:35,545
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that becomes your measure of the calmness.

427
00:28:37,862 --> 00:28:44,405
[SPEAKER_04]: The fact that I didn't have to get rid of this thing, which I used to always think it was bothered and I couldn't go to sleep if it was there.

428
00:28:44,666 --> 00:28:45,766
[SPEAKER_04]: All day, not bothering me.

429
00:28:45,806 --> 00:28:47,747
[SPEAKER_04]: The fact it was there was bothering me.

430
00:28:47,847 --> 00:28:49,768
[SPEAKER_04]: I was bothering myself with the thought of it.

431
00:28:50,409 --> 00:28:51,969
[SPEAKER_04]: Now, that has not changed.

432
00:28:52,150 --> 00:28:53,410
[SPEAKER_04]: Yet, I am unbothered.

433
00:28:54,051 --> 00:28:54,791
[SPEAKER_04]: Completely unbothered.

434
00:28:54,811 --> 00:28:55,912
[SPEAKER_02]: Amongst things that used to bother me.

435
00:28:55,952 --> 00:28:56,172
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

436
00:28:56,332 --> 00:28:58,533
[SPEAKER_04]: Amongst suffering, he ceases to suffer.

437
00:29:01,875 --> 00:29:11,938
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's that whole, like, the element, the kāgata, the one-pointedness, it just means higher place, unified higher place, safety.

438
00:29:13,059 --> 00:29:21,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Like the river being torched by a flaming torch, like, it's completely unaffected by... or the earth being... Oh, yeah, yeah, sure.

439
00:29:21,922 --> 00:29:26,103
[SPEAKER_04]: Whatever rubbish is thrown on the earth, it just cannot make a difference.

440
00:29:26,403 --> 00:29:30,765
[SPEAKER_04]: Whether the wind blows over feces or rubbish, it makes no difference to the wind.

441
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:35,346
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's... and it's also like peripheral awareness with this thing in front of you.

442
00:29:35,747 --> 00:29:37,347
[SPEAKER_04]: That's... yeah, that's kind of that direction.

443
00:29:37,507 --> 00:29:40,668
[SPEAKER_04]: That's... that's... that's where your shell is, the turtle.

444
00:29:41,368 --> 00:29:44,549
[SPEAKER_04]: But you gotta have to learn then... you have to start discerning these subtler things.

445
00:29:44,609 --> 00:29:48,611
[SPEAKER_04]: Yes, first physically and verbally is the way of acting out and reaching towards the jackal.

446
00:29:49,211 --> 00:29:55,213
[SPEAKER_04]: But then, do you cultivate the mind of... oh, I'm not acting towards sensuality, but mentally I'm happy about it.

447
00:29:56,557 --> 00:29:57,818
[SPEAKER_04]: You know, you're not enduring it.

448
00:29:58,278 --> 00:29:59,358
[SPEAKER_04]: You're already welcomed it.

449
00:30:00,299 --> 00:30:06,321
[SPEAKER_04]: Or, I'm not acting towards this aversive thing that's in front of me, but I really wish it harm.

450
00:30:08,882 --> 00:30:11,764
[SPEAKER_04]: So, it's like, oh, again, you're not enduring on the right level.

451
00:30:11,824 --> 00:30:12,804
[SPEAKER_03]: You're now averse.

452
00:30:13,164 --> 00:30:14,045
[SPEAKER_04]: Either way, exactly.

453
00:30:14,085 --> 00:30:18,266
[SPEAKER_04]: So, body, speech and mind need to be not acted out of.

454
00:30:18,387 --> 00:30:19,167
[SPEAKER_04]: And that's what it means.

455
00:30:21,356 --> 00:30:32,799
[SPEAKER_04]: So, if you discern that right, where the line is, that khanti is the highest tapas, is the highest purification, that endurance on the right level, that I keep saying, then you realize, okay, yeah, that is.

456
00:30:32,879 --> 00:30:33,559
[SPEAKER_04]: Protect that.

457
00:30:34,359 --> 00:30:36,580
[SPEAKER_04]: Don't lose sight of it, the balance of it.

458
00:30:37,660 --> 00:30:44,662
[SPEAKER_04]: And whatever comes, sensuality, ill-will, any of the hindrances, you will see through them.

459
00:30:46,062 --> 00:30:50,703
[SPEAKER_04]: And they will not hinder you to the... to whatever extent they might have arisen, it won't be hindering.

460
00:30:53,267 --> 00:31:01,170
[SPEAKER_04]: Because they only hinder you when you step, when you cross the line, when you went there, when you got involved by body, speech or mind.

461
00:31:03,731 --> 00:31:20,816
[SPEAKER_01]: To go back to the sutta about the all, about the I and forms, the ear and sounds and manner, the intellect and dhammas, so it's only possible really to to discern this relationship

462
00:31:24,025 --> 00:31:42,777
[SPEAKER_01]: If if one is secluded from sensuality, or will, because the... yeah, if one is involved in particular sounds, or particular sights, or particular phenomena... And that seclusion might start by being physically withdrawn,

463
00:31:43,419 --> 00:31:45,360
[SPEAKER_04]: Keeping the precepts, guiding of the sense doors.

464
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:54,504
[SPEAKER_04]: But then, that seclusion is really developed, when once you're physically withdrawn, you have your mind revolving around unwholesome things.

465
00:31:54,524 --> 00:31:55,825
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not trying to get rid of it.

466
00:31:56,825 --> 00:31:58,106
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not averse towards it.

467
00:31:58,646 --> 00:31:59,607
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not welcoming it.

468
00:32:00,047 --> 00:32:02,648
[SPEAKER_04]: You're actually patiently enduring those thoughts.

469
00:32:04,189 --> 00:32:06,650
[SPEAKER_04]: So, thoughts of sensuality, I must get rid of it.

470
00:32:06,910 --> 00:32:08,691
[SPEAKER_04]: No, I must not act towards it.

471
00:32:09,792 --> 00:32:10,632
[SPEAKER_04]: Why do I want to get rid of it?

472
00:32:10,652 --> 00:32:12,693
[SPEAKER_04]: Because I'm averse to the pain that it puts on me.

473
00:32:13,233 --> 00:32:14,794
[SPEAKER_04]: So, I'm not patient.

474
00:32:14,854 --> 00:32:16,255
[SPEAKER_04]: If there is aversion, you're not patient.

475
00:32:16,295 --> 00:32:17,655
[SPEAKER_04]: If there is lust, there's no patience.

476
00:32:17,915 --> 00:32:19,696
[SPEAKER_04]: If there is distraction, there is no patience.

477
00:32:19,836 --> 00:32:21,737
[SPEAKER_04]: There is no endurance on the right level.

478
00:32:22,768 --> 00:32:38,272
[SPEAKER_04]: And the reason why I keep kind of hammering this in is because a person might think, okay, yeah, so withdrawn from these things means I stop, I stop, obviously keep precepts, I stop acting out, then I go into seclusion and I stop thinking about these things and it will just fall off, fall... No, no, no.

479
00:32:38,312 --> 00:32:49,075
[SPEAKER_04]: That line is discerned when you have, sure, withdrawn yourself physically from the water, but then mentally, you actually realize, okay, but I have no say in mano and its own dhammas.

480
00:32:49,471 --> 00:32:53,394
[SPEAKER_04]: In the same sense, I have no say in eyes, in... in the sights, except restraint.

481
00:32:54,295 --> 00:32:55,496
[SPEAKER_04]: So, how do you restrain the mind?

482
00:32:55,576 --> 00:32:58,799
[SPEAKER_04]: How do you make mind not think images, which... when that's another image?

483
00:33:00,380 --> 00:33:14,132
[SPEAKER_04]: So, that's why it's much harder, as the Buddha said, to... to see this mind as not yours, and to experience this passion towards it, than other things that are inferior, that are more kind of coarser, because, yeah, you've been adhering to it, you've been confusing it for your own, and so on, for so long.

484
00:33:16,387 --> 00:33:17,910
[SPEAKER_04]: But that's where that line is.

485
00:33:18,391 --> 00:33:26,106
[SPEAKER_04]: So, once you have kept the precepts, are keeping the precepts, are withdrawn, living in seclusion, the mind will then come up with stuff, come up with...

486
00:33:26,883 --> 00:33:29,844
[SPEAKER_04]: Upsets, desires, things like that.

487
00:33:30,204 --> 00:33:35,405
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you deal with them, not by further taking your mind out of it and trying to stop thinking.

488
00:33:36,126 --> 00:33:41,427
[SPEAKER_04]: You deal with it by discerning the line for that jackal that is trying to get you involved.

489
00:33:41,767 --> 00:33:45,488
[SPEAKER_04]: Which means, initially, you're going to be involved and it's going to be unpleasant and you will want to act out of it.

490
00:33:45,828 --> 00:33:50,329
[SPEAKER_04]: And you want to go and resolve it or practice nostril concentration to stop thinking about it.

491
00:33:50,569 --> 00:33:52,270
[SPEAKER_04]: All of that because you're truly impatient.

492
00:33:53,202 --> 00:33:53,782
[SPEAKER_04]: But it's like, no.

493
00:33:54,663 --> 00:33:56,404
[SPEAKER_04]: I have been withdrawn physically.

494
00:33:56,424 --> 00:33:57,524
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm guarding my sense doors.

495
00:33:57,665 --> 00:33:58,725
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm not breaking the precepts.

496
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:01,427
[SPEAKER_04]: The virtue has been established, accomplished in.

497
00:34:01,947 --> 00:34:06,449
[SPEAKER_04]: I can take this pain of mind just revolving around stuff.

498
00:34:06,610 --> 00:34:06,810
[SPEAKER_04]: Fine.

499
00:34:07,030 --> 00:34:07,730
[SPEAKER_04]: Let him revolve.

500
00:34:07,950 --> 00:34:08,391
[SPEAKER_04]: It will have to...

501
00:34:08,711 --> 00:34:10,632
[SPEAKER_04]: Elephant from the jungle, pin down.

502
00:34:10,672 --> 00:34:11,812
[SPEAKER_04]: Do you think he's just going to immediately...

503
00:34:12,333 --> 00:34:12,693
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you.

504
00:34:12,853 --> 00:34:14,954
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, let's let's discuss what you want to train me.

505
00:34:15,234 --> 00:34:17,075
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm fully pliable right from the start.

506
00:34:17,216 --> 00:34:17,416
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

507
00:34:17,836 --> 00:34:20,437
[SPEAKER_04]: It's gonna try to break and kick and scream and kill you.

508
00:34:20,718 --> 00:34:22,799
[SPEAKER_04]: But it's like, well, no matter how much it hurts, you know.

509
00:34:22,899 --> 00:34:23,199
[SPEAKER_04]: No, no, no.

510
00:34:23,539 --> 00:34:24,220
[SPEAKER_04]: I pin him down.

511
00:34:24,420 --> 00:34:25,160
[SPEAKER_04]: He can't break this.

512
00:34:25,801 --> 00:34:28,162
[SPEAKER_04]: If I don't choose to let him out, he can't harm me.

513
00:34:29,523 --> 00:34:41,512
[SPEAKER_04]: If I don't choose to go back to sensuality, this mind, doesn't matter how many days... And that's why I say, like, often, you have to, at least initially, when you say, oh, I'll endure things on the right level, you have to accept the worst possible scenario.

514
00:34:42,072 --> 00:34:48,777
[SPEAKER_04]: Because the mind will come up, yeah, but if I don't resolve this doubt, but if I don't resolve this upset, forever it will be like that.

515
00:34:49,357 --> 00:34:49,537
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

516
00:34:50,218 --> 00:34:51,939
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm ready to endure it infinitely.

517
00:34:52,539 --> 00:34:56,222
[SPEAKER_04]: On that level, I shall not ever again cross the line and interfere with it.

518
00:34:57,048 --> 00:35:02,852
[SPEAKER_02]: If I don't transmute this sexual energy, my head's gonna explode or something.

519
00:35:02,872 --> 00:35:03,112
[SPEAKER_04]: Fine.

520
00:35:03,312 --> 00:35:05,694
[SPEAKER_04]: I will still not let the elephant go free.

521
00:35:07,335 --> 00:35:08,776
[SPEAKER_04]: Until it actually calms down.

522
00:35:09,276 --> 00:35:12,339
[SPEAKER_04]: Because all of these are tricks and traps of a jackal trying to get out.

523
00:35:12,659 --> 00:35:13,719
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, but I'll stay here forever.

524
00:35:14,340 --> 00:35:15,120
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, I better start running.

525
00:35:15,441 --> 00:35:16,702
[SPEAKER_04]: Oh, got me again.

526
00:35:17,042 --> 00:35:17,262
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

527
00:35:18,399 --> 00:35:19,280
[SPEAKER_04]: And it is that fear.

528
00:35:19,340 --> 00:35:22,883
[SPEAKER_04]: Even minor things, when you're in seclusion, minor things will be little doubts.

529
00:35:23,343 --> 00:35:26,265
[SPEAKER_04]: Or, hmm, he said... Did he mean this?

530
00:35:27,806 --> 00:35:30,208
[SPEAKER_04]: Did he mean... Three days later...

531
00:35:30,369 --> 00:35:31,009
[SPEAKER_04]: It's still there.

532
00:35:31,329 --> 00:35:37,314
[SPEAKER_04]: He meant that, and... And now, now I know everything else that would have followed, which never happened.

533
00:35:37,774 --> 00:35:42,798
[SPEAKER_04]: But then you realize, oh, then you go and talk to that person, and he never meant that, and now it's all fine.

534
00:35:42,898 --> 00:35:43,319
[SPEAKER_04]: No, it's not.

535
00:35:44,139 --> 00:35:45,219
[SPEAKER_04]: It's fine in a worldly sense.

536
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:47,320
[SPEAKER_04]: In an internal sense, you acted out.

537
00:35:47,740 --> 00:35:52,641
[SPEAKER_04]: And you use the the reference of the jackal and the world for where your safety is.

538
00:35:53,222 --> 00:35:54,082
[SPEAKER_04]: And there was a mistake.

539
00:35:54,382 --> 00:35:55,382
[SPEAKER_04]: Now it's going to come back again.

540
00:35:55,842 --> 00:35:57,863
[SPEAKER_04]: So, basically, you let the elephant go.

541
00:35:58,703 --> 00:35:59,783
[SPEAKER_04]: So, now you're going to start again.

542
00:35:59,983 --> 00:36:00,704
[SPEAKER_01]: By acting out of it.

543
00:36:00,764 --> 00:36:01,824
[SPEAKER_04]: By acting out of it, yeah.

544
00:36:02,644 --> 00:36:08,626
[SPEAKER_04]: So, what you want to do is recognize that such thoughts will inevitably be amplified in solitude.

545
00:36:09,186 --> 00:36:13,227
[SPEAKER_04]: And you have to accept the fact that, as I said, infinitely I will

546
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:20,147
[SPEAKER_04]: Endure this patiently, in that true sense of the word, on the right level, and not act out of it.

547
00:36:20,247 --> 00:36:21,268
[SPEAKER_04]: That's my sole job.

548
00:36:22,129 --> 00:36:23,411
[SPEAKER_03]: Not to cross this line.

549
00:36:23,631 --> 00:36:24,773
[SPEAKER_03]: Not to open this door.

550
00:36:25,575 --> 00:36:39,204
[SPEAKER_04]: And if you have set it up through physical withdrawal of the precepts, guarding of the sense doors, obviously the speech, physical withdrawal from company, seclusion, doesn't matter how much your mind will doubt and all the other hindrances, it will have to come down.

551
00:36:39,904 --> 00:36:41,505
[SPEAKER_04]: And again, that's why view is important.

552
00:36:41,565 --> 00:36:49,070
[SPEAKER_04]: If you don't see, if you don't... if you haven't taken a faith that it will have to come down, if you don't necessarily haven't seen it before, you won't do it.

553
00:36:49,630 --> 00:36:51,351
[SPEAKER_04]: Because there is no immediate verification.

554
