00:40:29,309 --> 00:40:31,471
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not aware of its counterweight.

611
00:40:31,832 --> 00:40:35,155
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not aware of its womb, or where it came from, so to speak.

612
00:40:35,215 --> 00:40:36,357
[SPEAKER_04]: What is the opposite to this?

613
00:40:36,377 --> 00:40:37,218
[SPEAKER_04]: You're not aware of it.

614
00:40:38,039 --> 00:40:41,823
[SPEAKER_04]: So, yoniso manasikāra, it's not a different way of attending to something new.

615
00:40:43,115 --> 00:40:52,158
[SPEAKER_04]: It's just learning how to not overly attend, so to speak, towards objects and discern the background in regard to them at the same time.

616
00:40:52,799 --> 00:40:53,319
[SPEAKER_04]: And what else?

617
00:40:53,939 --> 00:40:55,219
[SPEAKER_04]: That's exactly similar to the scale.

618
00:40:55,279 --> 00:40:56,940
[SPEAKER_04]: It's at the same time, it's even.

619
00:40:59,161 --> 00:41:00,321
[SPEAKER_01]: Not too much, not too little.

620
00:41:00,401 --> 00:41:00,561
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

621
